WEBVTT

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:09.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me all right? Teams is showing about three different microphones.</v>

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:18.039
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, you're clear. Before we start, whose new car is that in the car park? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.609
<v Tomasz Nowak>The blue one? Brave parking it under that tree.</v>

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.989
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. It'll have a different finish by lunchtime.</v>

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.450
<v Marcus Hale>More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Actual cake, not another packet of biscuits with a candle.</v>

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.450
<v Jamie Brennan>Finally, some useful operational information.</v>

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:45.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the catering meeting. It's Friday, 21 August. What's already closed out?</v>

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.979
<v Marcus Hale>I finished the repair on the HV board last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:55.820
<v Tomasz Nowak>Completely finished, yeah? Not sitting there waiting for the last bit?</v>

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.890
<v Marcus Hale>Completely. Nothing left over from that repair for today.</v>

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And I signed off the inspection on the trucks on Tuesday, so that's old business as well.</v>

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:15.629
<v Jamie Brennan>Same with the AC1. I already swapped the filter on the AC1 yesterday. That old line on the list is finished.</v>

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Those are completed items, not fresh jobs.</v>

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:27.670
<v Jamie Brennan>One observation from nights: noticed the air dryer was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:32.349
<v Aisha Begum>So a warm spell, rather than something that's still happening?</v>

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.780
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, exactly. Settled down. Just passing on what I saw, not asking for work on it.</v>

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:47.260
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on observations, I heard a slight rattle from the line 3 chiller. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:51.400
<v David Whitfield>Nothing definite enough to call a fault, then?</v>

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.599
<v Aisha Begum>No. Just a slight rattle. Not raising another job off that.</v>

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:02.140
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. The spare parts order is separate from that noise, just so we don't muddle them up.</v>

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:09.330
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll order spare parts for the line 3 chiller today at 2pm. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:15.120
<v Jamie Brennan>That's staying with Sarah Okafor, then, rather than dropping into my buying list?</v>

00:02:16.789 --> 00:02:23.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, with me. I'll place the order today at 2pm; no need to turn it into an emergency.</v>

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, understood. I won't duplicate the order.</v>

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:35.419
<v David Whitfield>On the subject of parts, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT1 fuel valve. Still blocked on that.</v>

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. That's a blocked status update, not another chase we're allocating this morning.</v>

00:02:43.169 --> 00:02:46.319
<v David Whitfield>Correct. Still no confirmed delivery, that's all I've got.</v>

00:02:47.729 --> 00:02:52.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:55.009 --> 00:03:00.610
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, um, the sensor calibration itself, rather than treating that warm spell as a new fault?</v>

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:08.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer. That's the top-priority job; the nights observation is separate.</v>

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.849
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer, top priority.</v>

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:22.240
<v Grace Liu>My blocked one hasn't changed either. Can't get to the IM1 hydraulic unit until production gives us a window.</v>

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:29.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. No window, no access. We're not treating that as a job to start today.</v>

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:34.180
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Just making the restriction clear, not promising anything on it.</v>

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:42.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Davey, can you chase the purchase order for the CT1 on Friday, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:47.120
<v David Whitfield>On Friday as in today, yeah? Not next Friday?</v>

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:53.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today, Friday. Just the CT1 purchase order, if you've got a spare minute. It's low priority.</v>

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.340
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the CT1 on Friday, today. Understood, spare-minute job.</v>

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:05.360
<v Jamie Brennan>Purchase order, not a delivery confirmation. Those two keep getting mixed together in conversation.</v>

00:04:05.669 --> 00:04:07.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Right, the sign-off next.</v>

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:14.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus Hale, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 TCU tomorrow at 9:30?</v>

00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:19.610
<v Marcus Hale>Tomorrow at 9:30, so Saturday morning? Just checking I've heard that properly.</v>

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:25.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Saturday. Tomorrow at 9:30 for the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 TCU.</v>

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:32.420
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, accepted. I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 TCU tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:34.269 --> 00:04:38.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Clear. I heard tomorrow as well, before anyone blames the headset.</v>

00:04:40.339 --> 00:04:45.240
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll schedule downtime for the GT2 Number 2 Bearing with production next week.</v>

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:53.779
<v Marcus Hale>That's agreeing the downtime with them next week, not saying the bearing work itself is definitely next week?</v>

00:04:54.319 --> 00:05:00.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. I'll do the scheduling with production next week. We're not agreeing a bearing-work date on this call.</v>

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.050
<v David Whitfield>Okay, scheduling sits with Sarah Okafor. No assumed strip-down date.</v>

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:06.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, that's mine.</v>

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:13.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Then there's the contractor booking for the turbine one. We need that booking made this morning.</v>

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Davey, can you book a contractor to look at the turbine one this morning?</v>

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:32.199
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, no, I can't take that booking on this morning. I haven't got the availability for it. The little CT1 chase is one thing, but I can't commit to this as well.</v>

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough, better to say now. I'll hand that one over.</v>

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:44.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you take it instead and book a contractor to look at the turbine one this morning?</v>

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:52.160
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll take that from Davey. I'll book a contractor to look at the turbine one this morning.</v>

00:05:53.189 --> 00:05:56.339
<v David Whitfield>Cheers, Grace. That's off me and with you, then.</v>

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:05.800
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, before we finish—we were going to replace the belt on the MV01, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:10.689
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, the belt replacement isn't on today's work. That's the old plan?</v>

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.949
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, old plan. Deferred to next month, nothing to pick up today.</v>

00:06:17.329 --> 00:06:26.779
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And to keep the order of importance clear, the Compressed Air Dryer sensor recalibration is top priority. Not the spare parts order or the purchase-order chase.</v>

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.569
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, clear. I've got the recalibration.</v>

00:06:31.079 --> 00:06:34.579
<v Marcus Hale>And the cake remains an observation, not an assigned action?</v>

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:40.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Definitely no owner or completion target for the cake. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
